<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Unihold year earnings rise, upbeat on 1997.</title>
<headline>Unihold year earnings rise, upbeat on 1997.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   27.7	  vs 21.6</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     26.1	  vs 23.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 11.0	  vs 10.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   11.67	 vs 14.22</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   14.91	 vs 22.63</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.86	  vs 8.01</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   5.38	  vs 1.07 received</p>
<p>    Turnover		  226.08	vs 155.86</p>
<p>Div payable March 28</p>
<p>on register March 7</p>
<p>Full name: Unihold Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Engineering group Unihold said it was targeting organic growth in EPS for 1997 of 20 percent after budgeting for an increase im the effective tax rate to 24 percent. It added it was negotiating various possible acquisitions in high growth areas.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
